504	    <h3>Contradictions and observations</h3>
505	    <ul>
506	      <li><b>Contradiction — how long a failure toast stays.</b> system-states.md § Toast says a toast “disappears on its own”; <code>frontend/src/components/ui/Toast.tsx</code> keeps error toasts until they are dismissed. The failure toasts here (C-18) are drawn with their dismiss button, as the code behaves, and the unchanged screen carries the lasting fact. This decides how long the R-10 message stays; the screen specification should settle it.</li>
507	      <li><b>Contradiction — the empty-state primitive.</b> system-states.md § Components lists <code>EmptyState</code>; <code>Feedback.tsx</code> records that it was removed (requirements.md § Impact analysis already notes this). The empty sentence is drawn inline, as the guestbook's is (design/delta/architecture.md decision 5).</li>
508	      <li><b>Contradiction — sizes off the scale.</b> system-states.md § Tokens allows sizes outside the Tailwind scale (“<code>rounded-[14px]</code> … allowed”); theme.css § Radii and conventions.md § Frontend require a token or the scale. This page uses tokens and scale steps only.</li>
509	      <li><b>Observation — colours outside theme.css in two live primitives.</b> The toast glyphs use Tailwind's own green, amber and red, and the dialog's backdrop is black at 45%, against system-states.md § Tokens (“named tokens only”). They are drawn here with tokens (an inverse tick, a danger dot, ink at 45%). This change does not touch them.</li>
510	      <li><b>Observation — field edges.</b> Field edges use <code>--color-hairline</code>, as on the guestbook, which is below the 3:1 WCAG 1.4.11 asks of a control's edge. The focus ring marks the field while it is focused. Only the new checkbox is given a stronger edge (C-12).</li>
511	      <li><b>Observation — typefaces.</b> This page loads nothing from the network, so Instrument Serif and Instrument Sans show only if installed. Otherwise the token stacks fall back to Georgia and the system sans, as the built screen does when the font host fails.</li>
512	    </ul>
